---
description: A service, controller, or repository does one job; further work is a new entity
globs: apps/api/app/**/*.py
alwaysApply: false
---

# Responsibility

A controller maps the request, calls a service, and maps the response. HTTP status belongs here. Domain rules do not.

A service does one job and does not take a session. `CampaignService` stores and syncs campaigns. Comparing a stored row with Keitaro is `CampaignMatchService`. The flow bodies are `CampaignStreamService`. The Admin API call is `KeitaroService`.

A repository persists one table. It does not decide a match, a share split, a dirty flag, which rows are stale, an HTTP status, or a Keitaro call. `CampaignRepository` is the only writer of campaign rows. The stream, offer, and stream-offer repositories are the only writers of those tables. `HealthRepository` runs the reachability query. `HealthService` owns the ok status.

When a method takes on a second job, that job is a new entity in its own file. A short private helper used only by that entity may stay.

```python
# Bad: the campaign service both stores the row and decides the flow schema
def create(self, draft: CampaignDraft) -> Campaign:
    body = {"schema": "redirect", "action_payload": "https://www.google.com"}

# Good: the stream service owns the flow body
country_stream_id = self._keitaro.create_stream(self._streams.country(campaign_id, draft.country))
```
